After the imports, we have a function named `App()`, which defines the structure of the `App` component. Whereas most of the JavaScript community prefers names like `helloWorld`, React components use Pascal case (or upper camel case) variable names, like `HelloWorld`, to make it clear that a given JSX element is a React component and not a regular HTML tag. If you were to rename the `App()` function to `app()`, your browser would throw an error.

